<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the Pass-1 remediations that are about the model. The GIF caption is ASCII. Orientation KS is now a 4000-pixel magnitude-weighted sample (0.4605), reported beside the coarser 12-bin KS. The fractional gap (lambda_sigma - lambda_c) / lambda_c is 1.5% at r = 9 and 4.8% at the operating ratio r = 10, so the expressed wavelength moves toward the critical wavenumber as the system approaches onset. D_u sweep Pearson r remains 0.989 (RMSE 0.41 px). Species-card CV similarity remains 79.0 (12 frames, 640×520). The species card is still not an ocellar micrograph, and there is still one assessor. Overall 85.9/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 410960 B, 1248×984 px, artifact_sha256 770698a0f143c649e77e3c6e02e3cdc27a9bf18d810befd7f6d6f5891850e9dd (sha256 770698a0f143c649e77e3c6e02e3cdc27a9bf18d810befd7f6d6f5891850e9dd), spec_fingerprint 2f4962a2f9aad429899235fd1af99851f464c94cb46349fdccbc4240f10a01bb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2f4962a2f9aad429899235fd1af99851f464c94cb46349fdccbc4240f10a01bb; artifact_sha256: 770698a0f143c649e77e3c6e02e3cdc27a9bf18d810befd7f6d6f5891850e9dd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_americana_specimen.jpg=c14927be1f313896..., datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=54ba0c292c786355..., datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=1770ea1c999fdf81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v). | Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic, at body-color scale. | Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018 place ananassae in Sophophora and americana in the virilis radiation.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics at a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, Fourier semi-implicit integration. | Detail wavelengths 1.958, 2.117 and 1.900 µm from body-length exponent 0.35. | Near-onset gap at r = 9 compared with the operating gap at r = 10.; transfer_boundary: 2.117 µm is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not measure that length. | Affinis and ananassae are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not fossil ancestors.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the species card is an ocellar micrograph. | Does not claim the X–4 fusion or the red/brown puparium enters the reaction-diffusion equations. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present. | Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044 (Crossref 404).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Pixel-orientation KS is 0.46. A closer match would need a specimen micrograph of the ocellar pigment field, which was not available.",
        "remediation needed: R4 remains open: one species card and one assessor. The card is not an ocellar micrograph, so specimen-match stays at 78 rather than tracking the CV score of 79 upward into an anatomical claim." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.59e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

