<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) (Drosophila americana)",
        "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila americana morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila americana specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila americana" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the X–4 fusion or the red/brown puparium enters the reaction-diffusion equations.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044 (Crossref 404).",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the species card is an ocellar micrograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Detail wavelengths 1.958, 2.117 and 1.900 µm from body-length exponent 0.35.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Near-onset gap at r = 9 compared with the operating gap at r = 10.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics at a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, Fourier semi-implicit integration.",
        "reported_in_source: Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018 place ananassae in Sophophora and americana in the virilis radiation.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v).",
        "reported_in_source: Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic, at body-color scale.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.117 µm is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not measure that length.",
        "transfer_boundary: Affinis and ananassae are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not fossil ancestors." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila americana (North American Riparian Willow Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila americana; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v). | Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic, at body-color scale. | Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018 place ananassae in Sophophora and americana in the virilis radiation.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics at a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, Fourier semi-implicit integration. | Detail wavelengths 1.958, 2.117 and 1.900 µm from body-length exponent 0.35. | Near-onset gap at r = 9 compared with the operating gap at r = 10.; transfer_boundary: 2.117 µm is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not measure that length. | Affinis and ananassae are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not fossil ancestors.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the species card is an ocellar micrograph. | Does not claim the X–4 fusion or the red/brown puparium enters the reaction-diffusion equations. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present. | Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044 (Crossref 404).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
